Client initialization — reads OPENAI_API_KEY and OPENAI_API_BASE via os.environ.get(...), which the source /root/.bash_profile step populates.

compare(item1: str, item2: str) -> str — exact signature required by the spec; the prompt is parameterized with {item1} and {item2}.

Prompt constraints — explicitly says "only the chip used" and "in one word only."

API call parameters — model="gpt-5.6-luna", messages=[{"role": "user", "content": prompt}], max_tokens=100, temperature=0.5.

response variable — the spec says "Store the result in a variable named response," so the top-level call assigns to response and print(response) outputs the one-word comparison.

File location — /root/openaiproject/compare.py.

